## To release a new version, edit the version in the two lines below and nothing else.
## |cRRGGBB...|r in Title and Author colours them in the in-game add-on list; the version
## is read back through that markup, so it can sit inside or outside the colour.
## The settings panel takes its version from ## Title; the name itself is fixed in Main.lua.
## Title: |cFF69B4PB’s NamePlateChanger|r 1.1.0
## Author: |cFF69B4PinkBanther|r
## Description: Adjusts the font of the names above characters' heads -- size, typeface and outline. The game draws those nametags itself, so their line order cannot be changed by an add-on; the font can.
## Version: 1.1.0
## APIVersion: 101050 101051
## DependsOn: LibHarvensAddonSettings>=20106
## Both previous names' saved variables are still declared so the untouched nameplate font
## captured under them can be migrated. Without that the add-on captures the *modified* font
## as the original and "reset" never gets back to stock -- which is exactly what happened on
## the first rename. Safe to drop a few versions from now.
## SavedVariables: PBsNamePlateChanger_Data PBsNamePlateFontChanger_Data PBsNameTagOptimizer_Data

lang/strings.lua
lang/$(language).lua

Main.lua
Settings.lua

